doc:
The number of characteristic eigenvalues in a set, counted with
algebraic multiplicity. Source: Horn–Johnson (2013), Theorem 6.1.1;
the characteristic-root multiset includes every repeated root.

A complete characteristic factorization computes root counts by the
number of list entries in the set. Source: Horn–Johnson (2013), Theorem 6.1.1;
this explicitly connects index counts to algebraic multiplicities.

Inserting a zero coupling in a diagonal rank-one update restores an
uncoupled scalar characteristic factor. Horn–Johnson 2013, Theorem 4.3.26;
repeated-root converse-interlacing restoration helper.

Relabeling every leading coordinate of a diagonal arrowhead leaves its
characteristic polynomial unchanged. Source: permutation similarity;
helper for the arbitrary-finite-shape converse-interlacing constructions.

