doc:
The endpoint arctangent value of a nonreal unit-circle point gives the square-wave sign.
Source: the principal complex logarithm and Cayley transform;
helper for `chebyshev-series-abs-sign`.

`-ε - (1 - ε) log(1 - ε) ≤ -ε²/2` for `0 ≤ ε < 1`. Proof: `g(ε) = (1-ε)log(1-ε) + ε - ε²/2`
vanishes at `0` and has derivative `-log(1-ε) - ε ≥ 0`. Tropp 2012, Rem 5.3 (lower tail);
atlas `matrix-chernoff-sampling` (helper).

The leading conjugated perturbation entry is exactly the normalized
left–right perturbation pairing. Source: Horn–Johnson (2013), Theorem 6.3.12;
for complex left columns use their conjugate row in the hypotheses.

A squared finite Fourier sum equals the sum of successive Dirichlet kernels.
Source: Fejér's finite kernel identity, ATAP Exercise 6.6;
operator rederivations `polyseries:fejerkernel`.

